To determine how long it will take for the fog bank to cover the entire city, we start with the information that it takes 324 minutes to cover 3 miles of the city. The total distance of the city is 63 miles.

First, we calculate the time required per mile:
\[
\text{Time per mile} = \frac{\text{Total time}}{\text{Distance covered}}
= \frac{324 \text{ minutes}}{3 \text{ miles}}
= 108 \text{ minutes per mile}
\]

Next, we need to find out how much time it will take to cover the entire 63-mile city:
\[
\text{Total time for the city} = \text{Time per mile} \times \text{Total distance}
= 108 \text{ minutes per mile} \times 63 \text{ miles}
= 6804 \text{ minutes}
\]

Thus, it will take **6804 minutes** for the fog bank to cover the whole city. Answer: 6804 minutes.
